From a02534261070998be2a4421ef345f567ee782523 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Akhil <gamepadadmin01@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 18:40:15 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Phase 0: remove the Supabase account prototype and its
 unsafe tooling

The account prototype was never wired into App.tsx (App.tsx is byte-identical
to the hlooo baseline), so none of this code ever rendered. What it did do was
ship 222 KB of Supabase SDK and a broken AuthProvider into every APK.

Removed:
- AuthContext/AuthModal/EditProfileModal/ProfileButton/TabProfile/ProfileSection
  ProfileSection claimed "Cloud Sync Active - Your gamepads are backed up" with
  no backend. TabProfile hardcoded layout counts, an always-on "Android Phone"
  device row, an invented "Standard Account" tier, and themes/controller styles
  that no engine implements.
- FirstLaunchIntro: a launch-time sign-in gate, the pattern we explicitly reject.
- supabaseClient.ts + @supabase/supabase-js: identity moves to our own Railway
  backend, which already has scrypt sessions, email verification and audit logs.
- inject.js / injectMain.js / fixApp.js: regex patchers for App.tsx. Two of the
  five anchors could never match (ProfileButton is absent; the portal anchor uses
  \n against a CRLF file), and fixApp.js exists only to repair the ~60 lines an
  earlier run deleted. App.tsx is edited surgically from now on, never by regex.

AuthContext shipped `setIsGuest(true)` with no such setter - present verbatim in
the installed APK as `g=()=>{setIsGuest(!0),v()}`. The build script is `vite
build` with no `tsc`, so it compiled clean.

Kept GuestAccountMenu.tsx: no auth dependency, matches the spec, no fake data.

Also drops --accept-data-loss from the backend prestart. It ran `prisma db push
--accept-data-loss` on every deploy, free to drop columns and tables; that is
not acceptable once User and Layout hold customer data. Full migration baseline
lands with the Railway database move.

Bundle: 783,892 -> 561,870 bytes. Verified zero occurrences of supabase,
signInWithPassword, auth_user and setIsGuest in the built output; Android
assets bundle re-synced and hash-matched.
